  "description": "IBOLAM crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C58 H84 N8 O10 Pr4,4(C4 H8 O1). From the CIF bond table, Pr1 (Pr) has 4 O neighbors; Pr2 (Pr) has 6 O neighbors; Pr2B (Pr) has 6 O neighbors; Pr1B (Pr) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.771-4.050 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.04-111.65°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [η5-CpPr2(L1)2(μ-OH)]2·4THF (C74H116N8O14Pr4; L1 = acacen).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
